Standalone gateway connection-test ownership
============================================

GatewayService.test_connection owns the adapter it creates and attempts
disconnect in a finally block after success, a failed AdapterResult, an
exception, malformed result handling or task cancellation. Saved-gateway
tests delegate to the same method and retain this ownership behavior.
The vendor adapter context-manager contract and shared-context operations
are unchanged. No extra connection or repeated authentication is introduced.

An ordinary exception from disconnect does not replace the original test
result or cancellation. The service records a fixed warning without the
cleanup exception text. Other adapter/infrastructure log behavior is not
changed. Existing low-level cleanup remains compatible, including OPNsense
test finalization and MikroTik cleanup on HTTP401.

Qualification includes actual HTTPX/vendor clients and TLS keepalive peers,
authentication refusal, peer disconnect and real asyncio cancellation.
Closure is observed before the probe's fallback cleanup. The old OpenWRT
success case retains an open keepalive connection; service-owned cleanup
closes it. Appliance payloads are synthetic, the fixture hostname and trust
CA are local overrides, and no device write is performed. Additional unit
cases exercise result-processing errors and ordinary cleanup exceptions.

Cleanup remains best effort when an underlying close operation itself fails.
Repeated cancellation, concurrent use of one adapter, permanently blocked
close calls, server-side session revocation and physical device acceptance
are not established. This change does not sanitize every adapter diagnostic,
revalidate caller permissions after device I/O or fix other standalone users
of a low-level client. Those remain separate boundaries.

Connection-test message and service-exception log projection is covered in
GATEWAY-TEST-DIAGNOSTICS. Other adapter logs and provider metadata remain
outside that diagnostic boundary.
